course: dictionary
lesson: 11468
title: Facing adversity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adversity is a noun for a hard or unlucky time, full of problems and troubles. You do not need to know the word already. Read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The little team faced adversity with courage and never gave up.» The team had a hard time, and they stayed brave, so adversity must mean difficulties.
explain: Adversity can be a whole hard time, like illness or being poor, or one unlucky event. Look for plurals too. «Losing his home was one of the many adversities he had to face.» Adversities means several hard events. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: You will often see adversity in phrases. «In the face of adversity» means while facing problems. «Overcome adversity» means get through hard times and beat them. «Triumph over adversity» means win in the end, after a struggle. Stories and history books use these phrases to show courage and patience.
explain: Adversity is linked to resilience, which means bouncing back after hard times. «Maya showed great patience in the face of adversity.» Patience and courage are clues that the adversity was difficult but she kept going. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Adversity means a very hard or unlucky time, full of problems and troubles.
fact: The plural of adversity is adversities, and it means several hard events or misfortunes.
fact: «Overcome adversity» means get through hard times and beat them.
fact: «In the face of adversity» means while facing hard times, often with courage.
fact: Resilience means getting through hard times and bouncing back, and it is closely linked to adversity.
exercise: «The little team faced adversity with courage and never gave up.» What does adversity mean here? | A sunny day at the beach | A game with a ball | *A hard and difficult time | A happy party
exercise: «Losing his home was one of the many adversities he had to face.» What is the plural of adversity? | adversity | advice | advert | *adversities
exercise: In stories, heroes often «overcome adversity». What does overcome adversity mean? | To ask for help with homework | *To get through hard times and beat them | To make hard times worse | To run away from every problem
exercise: «Despite the hardship of a long illness, Ben kept smiling.» Which word is closest in meaning to hardship? | *adversity | sunshine | prize | holiday
exercise: Why do stories often show heroes overcoming adversity? | To show that nothing ever goes wrong | *To show courage and patience | To show they never had any troubles | To make the story boring
test: «The family faced many adversities after the flood, but they stayed kind to each other.» What does adversities mean here? | Pleasant walks by the river | Happy surprises | Small jobs around the house | *Hard events and misfortunes
test: Which phrase means facing problems while staying brave? | A bowl of adversity | Adversity is my favourite colour | Adversity on a sunny day | *In the face of adversity
exam: Which word means a very hard or unlucky time, full of problems and troubles? | adventure | *adversity | advice | advert
